X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Metrotrails": "https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/314502228/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_metrotrails
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_314502228@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260503T035608Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260503T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260503T180000
SUMMARY:Pompton Transportation History Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this 15 mile loop hike along the Pompton River Watershed and f
 eaturing long stretches of the Morris Canal and its Pompton Feeder\, as we
 ll as the former Greenwood Lake Branch of the Erie Railroad. As such\, thi
 s hike fits into our Passaic Watershed series\, our Greenwood Lake Branch 
 series\, as well as a return to the Morris Canal series because new segmen
 ts have been improved.\nNOTE: Wolfson's Market is right across from the pa
 rking. Good for buying supplies or as a guide for where to go.\nAfter meet
 ing at Aqueduct Park\, we'll walk a little over two miles on back streets 
 to the south along the Pompton River to where we left off at the old Twin 
 Bridges. From there\, we walk a short distance to the Morris Canal Greenwa
 y.\nWe'll follow the main canal to the Pompton Feeder Canal\, and begin fo
 llowing that north.\nMost of this is a grassy trail\, a very pleasant walk
  along the Pompton River and through little neighborhoods.\nWe'll continue
  up the Pompton Feeder to Pompton Plains Crossroad where we'll head west a
  bit\, past the Stop and Shop\, to the Greenwood Lake Branch of the Erie R
 ailroad\, now a new rail trail.\nWe'll follow the rail bed just about back
  to the beginning.\nThis should be a very pleasant hike with only minimal 
 roads and a lot of nice easy walkway.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8
 374
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/314502228/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260427T035751Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260427T035751Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
