SUMMARY:SMC Trail Work Volunteer Day
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\n**TRAIL WO
 RK** will continue work on the Lenape Trail reroute below the Beech Brook 
 Cascades. The steps are in (see photo)\, but final tread improvements on s
 witchbacks and throughout are needed. We will meet at the Dog Park (11 Bea
 r Lane) and head down to the Lenape trail from there.\n\nTrail work is phy
 sically challenging but very satisfying as we use hand tools to build and 
 repair trails. Participants must be 15+ years. Those younger than 18 must 
 be accompanied by an adult. Participants should wear long pants due to [ti
 cks](https://www.somocon.org/?page_id=193928&fb) and sturdy shoes\, and br
 ing gloves (though backup gloves will be available). Tools\, water\, and a
  snack will be provided. (Registration is not required though if you sign 
 up on Meetup\, it helps us know how many tools to bring.)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/314526367/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260428T151701Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T151701Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
