LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T185013Z
UID:10139772-1777824000-1777829400@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:St. James Spring Chamber Music Concert
DESCRIPTION:What began as a chance conversation in Anderson Park between oboist Randall Wolfgang and Reverend Melissa Hall has grown into one of Montclair’s most delightful musical traditions. Since 2020\, world‑class musicians from the Ballet\, Opera\, Philharmonic\, and Broadway have joined Randall to fill St. James with chamber music twice a year. Join us for the Spring Concert on Sunday\, May 3 at 4 PM\, featuring Dvořák’s Serenade for Winds and Irving Fine’s Partita for Wind Quintet — performed by thirteen exceptional artists. Admission is free; donations are welcome to help sustain this inspiring series. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/st-james-spring-chamber-music-concert/
LOCATION:St. James Episcopal Church\, Upper Montclair\, 581 Valley Road\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07043\, United States
CATEGORIES:Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IMG_4142-1-scaled.jpeg
