DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T210000
DTSTAMP:20260502T235403
CREATED:20260429T151630Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260429T151630Z
UID:10139777-1778173200-1778187600@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:May Free First Thursday: Rhythms of Asia
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the rich artistic traditions and dynamic cultures of Asia at this month’s Free First Thursday: Rhythms of Asia\, presented by TD Bank! \nAdmission is FREE\, but registration is required. \nMusic \n5–9 p.m. | Leir Hall \nEnjoy an energizing set from guest DJ SunnyG as he brings the rhythms of Asia to life. \n  \nMAM Learning Lab \n5:30–8:30 p.m. | Learning Lab\, 3rd Floor \nGet a beautiful Mehndi (Henna) design to show off for the rest of the night\, courtesy of TD Bank. \n  \nArt Activity: Origami \n5:30–8:30 p.m. | Geyer Studio \nLearn the intricate art of origami with expert instruction from artist Nobuko Okabe. Open to all ages; drop in anytime! \n  \nDisability Pride Art Making  \n5:30-8:30 p.m. | Studio A \nCreate signs\, banners\, or wearable art to celebrate disability pride and civil rights.\nAll materials provided. Bring your art to the 6th Annual Montclair Disability Pride Parade and Community Inclusion Fair\, Saturday\, May 30.\nParade/Fair (location to be announced). \n  \nMehndi (Henna) Tables \n5:30-8:30 p.m. | Leir Hall \nGet a beautiful Mehndi (Henna) design to show off for the rest of the night\, courtesy of TD Bank. \n  \nDocent Gallery Tour \n6:30 p.m. | Meet at Cornerstone Café \nEnjoy a guided tour of Interwoven Power: Native Knowledge / Native Art with one of MAM’s knowledgeable docents. \n  \nWelcome and Introductions \n6:45 p.m. | Leir Hall \n  \nPerformance \n7-8 p.m. | Leir Hall \nKulture Kool The South Asian Cultural Center of Rutherford\, New Jersey presents a vibrant evening of Bollywood fun! Enjoy dazzling performances by talented students and a BollyX dance-along. \n  \nDocent Gallery Tour \n7:30 p.m. | Meet at Cornerstone Café \nTour of See It Now: Contemporary Art from the Ann and Mel Schaffer Collection \nEat & Drink \n\nCash (& credit) Bar with specialty cocktail + other beverages\nMs. Fu Yummy Food Truck at MAM’s side entrance\nCornerstone Café offers hot coffee and tasty treats and will be open from 5-7 p.m.\n\nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/may-free-first-thursday-rhythms-of-asia/
