SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nSmall Lives in Big Cities film 
 series\; Mahanagar (1963)—Calcutta.\n\nABOUT THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN 
 - I am a lifelong film fanatic who eats\, breathes\, sleeps and drinks 
 movies. I have studied with Donald Spoto at the New School in NYC and have 
 a BA and MA in Speech and Theatre from MSU. I have also worked as an actor 
 and have directed several plays in local regional and community theaters\, 
 including the Whole Theatre in Montclair and the Paper Mill Playhouse in 
 Millburn\, NJ. I am currently working as an adjunct professor teaching\, 
 among other courses\, Introduction to Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis 
 class is run by the MILL. Please register for classes directly through 
 their website here.\n\nFor questions about MILL classes please call 
 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible through a partnership between 
 the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16678763
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678763
END:VEVENT
