DESCRIPTION:**Midday MeetUp - Blueberries\, New Jersey’s Wonder Fruit** 
   \nA monthly gathering to make connections and learn together.  \n11:45am
  Catered Lunch (free)  \n12:30pm Featured Program   \n  \nSpeaker: Food hi
 storian\, Judith Krall-Russo  \n  \nThe cultivated blueberry has its roots
  in the Pinelands of New Jersey. Elizabeth White along with Dr. Fredrick C
 oville\, proved that the “swamp huckleberry” could be cultivated. Lear
 n the history of this fascinating berry and the contributions Elizabeth Wh
 ite of Whitesbog made to their cultivation. Today the blueberry is touted 
 as the wonder fruit with a host of healthful benefits. Learn about the his
 tory\, health benefits and a variety of ways to prepare and savor these be
 rries.  \n  \n**Cost:** FREE or Suggested Donation of $10 per person to of
 fset costs. (Bill My Account is only open to Shomrei Members)  \n  \n**RSV
 P:** Required so we know how much food to buy.  \nhttps://shomrei.easyshul
 .com/events/6967e4b6368f110026c0c460  \n  \n**\\***Members &amp\; PreSchoo
 l Families should use their fob to access the building.   \n  \nFull_Seaso
 n_Schedule_for_Midday_MeetUps: https://shomrei.org/calendar/midday-meetup-
 calendar  \n  \n**Questions?** Contact June Zimmerman\,   \nVP for Program
 ming  \njzimmerman@shomrei.org  \n  \n\\#middaymeetup\n\n
