SUMMARY:The Iconic Contralto: Marian Anderson Online NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nMarian Anderson was a celebrated American singer and a pivotal 
 civil rights figure. Renowned for her rich voice\, she broke racial 
 barriers in classical music\, famously singing at the Lincoln Memorial in 
 1939 after being denied a venue by the Daughters of the American 
 Revolution. She was the first African American to perform at the 
 Metropolitan Opera.\n\nJoin this class to prepare you for our outing\, My 
 Lord\, What a Night!\, a theatrical performance at the George Street 
 Playhouse in New Brunswick on Sunday\, May 17. An acclaimed play by Deborah 
 Brevoort dramatizing the friendship between famed singer Marian Anderson 
 and Albert Einstein\, My Lord\, What a Night! explores their response to 
 racism after Anderson was denied a hotel room in Princeton\, NJ\, and 
 Einstein hosted her\, setting the stage for her historic civil rights 
 activism.
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Music, Talk
UID:LibCal-10306-16582043
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16582043
END:VEVENT
