SUMMARY:Egypt: Beyond The Pyramids NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nMost people picture Egypt as pyramids\, pharaohs\, and ancient 
 temples. But Egypt is also the White Desert's surreal rock formations\, 
 salt lakes shimmering in Siwa Oasis\, and valleys where whale fossils 
 remain from a long-vanished sea. It's the unexpected green of Al-Azhar Park 
 in the heart of Cairo\, the ornate grandeur of a forgotten palace on the 
 Nile\, and the Bibliotheca Alexandrina\, a modern landmark inspired by one 
 of history’s most famous libraries. Whether you’re planning a trip or 
 curious about Egypt beyond the usual sights\, come discover a side that's 
 often overlooked.\n\nIn this engaging talk\, journalist and MSU professor 
 Jenny Montasir\, who lived and worked in Egypt for four years\, offers a 
 vivid look at both ancient landmarks and contemporary life. Whether you're 
 a traveler\, history enthusiast\, or simply curious about Egyptian 
 culture\, this session brings Egypt to life through stories\, visuals\, and 
 firsthand experience.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16497378
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16497378
END:VEVENT
