SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260503T035607Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T133000
SUMMARY:SQL Server 2025: The Future of Data Starts Here
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Data Driven\nSQL Server 2025 is more than just an upgrad
 e—it’s a leap forward. From becoming an AI-ready database to deliverin
 g modern development tools\, this release is packed with innovations that 
 redefine performance\, scalability\, and productivity.\n\nIn this session\
 , you’ll see demos and practical examples showcasing a wide range of enh
 ancements\, including:\n\nImproved JSON handling\nT‑SQL REST API integra
 tion\nExpanded T‑SQL functionality\, including fuzzy string matching and
  regular expression support\nTime‑bound Extended Events\nChange event st
 reaming for real‑time data integration\nMirroring in Microsoft Fabric\nU
 pdates to change tracking and columnstore indexes\n\nWhether you’re a de
 veloper\, DBA\, or architect\, this session will help you understand where
  SQL Server 2025 fits into your broader data platform strategy. Join us to
  explore what’s new and improved in SQL Server 2025!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/cloud-data-driven/events/314133019/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260405T143339Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260405T143339Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairfoundation Calendar Of Events": "https://montclairfoundation.org/event/mill-whats-in-bloom/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairfoundation_calendar_of_events
X-SOURCE:Montclair Foundation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T143000
DTSTAMP:20260502T235612
CREATED:20260331T144550Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260331T224344Z
UID:10007529-1779370200-1779373800@montclairfoundation.org
SUMMARY:MILL What's in bloom?
DESCRIPTION:These classes are a Partner Program with the Montclair Institute for Lifelong Learning. To register please visit: http://schedulesplus.com/montclair/kiosk \nThursdays\, 1:30 PM – 2:30 PM \nMay 21 – What’s in Bloom Tour – Join Laura Roberts\, Director of Horticulture at Van Vleck\, for a journey through the beauty of the season. Discover enchanting details and appreciate majestic specimens. Outdoor tour\, so please dress for the weather with appropriate footwear. (Outdoor Program\, indoors if inclement weather) \nMay 28 – Focus on Flowers Walk – Spend an afternoon in the garden taking a close-up look at the beauty of flowers. After learning about each flower\, discover helpful hints in capturing photos using your phone or camera. Instructors: Laura Roberts and Tracey Diamond (Outdoor Program\, indoors if inclement weather) \nJune 4 – Birds of Prey Program – Flat Rock Brook Nature Center will visit Van Vleck with live birds of prey. Learn fascinating facts about these incredible creatures that live right here in New Jersey. (Indoor Program) \nJune 11 – Late Spring Blooming Tree tour – This guided tree identification walk led by Laura Roberts will focus on spring-blooming trees. This is an outdoor tour\, so please dress for the weather with appropriate footwear. (Outdoor Program\, indoors if inclement weather) \nJune 18 – Birds and Art – We’ll learn about some of our favorite resident birds at Van Vleck with Naturalist Jenny Aley and discuss their summer activities. We will also explore our creative side with a simple painting or sketching activity that will help us identify some of our beautiful native birds. No experience necessary – all levels of birders and artists welcome! (Indoor Program) \nJune 25th – Mindfulness in the Garden – Jodi Brooks will guide us through very gentle stretching & breathwork\, and an outdoor contemplative garden walk. This is a practice of slowing down\, cultivating quiet and paying attention to our senses. All levels are welcome. No experience needed. Cold or rainy weather – class will be held indoors\, with a short walk outdoors (weather permitting). (Outdoor Program\, indoors if inclement weather)
URL:https://montclairfoundation.org/event/mill-whats-in-bloom/
LOCATION:Van Vleck House & Gardens\, 21 Van Vleck Street\, Montclair\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Classes,Adults
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairfoundation.org/content/uploads/2026/03/Helleborus-orientalis-Lenten-rose.jpg
END:VEVENT
